# $type

Shows a greeting and today's date. It needs no network.

## Layouts

| Layout | Shows |
|---|---|
| `greeting_date` (default) | the greeting, with the date below it |
| `greeting` | the greeting only, as large as fits |

## Settings

| Setting | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `greeting` | `Hello` | The text shown on the screen |

It suggests a refresh every hour.

In the config file (every other setting is in the [settings reference](https://txoof.github.io/PaperPi/settings/)):

```toml
[[plugin]]
id = "$type-1a2b3c4d"
type = "$type"
greeting = "Good morning"
```

Try it without a screen: `uv run paperpi render $type`.
